This modular design allows researchers to use the complete atlas or isolate individual descriptor families.




6. Scalable Configuration Space

RF configuration space is not naturally finite.

Unlike a fixed nuclear grid, RF systems contain many continuous or discretizable variables, including:





carrier frequency;




bandwidth;




transmit and receive power;




sampling rate;




phase;




timing;




modulation;




protocol;




antenna geometry;




channel model;




propagation distance;




relative speed;




Doppler shift;




SNR;




interference;




multipath;




weather;




mobility;




jamming;




receiver impairments.



The number of possible configurations therefore depends on the selected discretization grid.

A representative large-scale combinatorial grid may include:




Configuration Axis
Number of States


Signal classes
12


